From a1ae1a082b901a70d9135cb7b6352fbcbb10b444 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:18:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Keep unanswered orchestrator decisions agent-owned

Cause: three delivery-recovery paths promoted elapsed time or missing subscribers into human authority. The producer copied agent handoffs into needs_input requests. Direct database calls skipped tool pre-call skills/ask-gate, and the core shape validator accepted the populated fields; For-you correctly projected the invalidly authored request. Existing tests explicitly required this escalation.

Fix: preserve scheduled custody, original probe/deadline and owner; record one agent-owned recovery observation per ask. Retain pending owner notices on overdue budget/slot waits and failed wakes instead of consuming them passively. Genuine human-only requests remain separately authored with concrete action and scope.

Proof: observed M5 placement payload plus quota/offline/no-subscriber cases RED against original producer; retry custody RED before correction. GREEN: 32 consumer files, 678 passed. Actual plugin-boundary proof: core shape validation accepts historical payload while pre_tool_call holds it; real user-steps For-you projection excludes scheduled/no-request waits and includes explicit human asks. Full scripts/check passed. No downstream product source/launch/release gates changed.
